{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/956157-refinement-furnaces","id":956157,"title":"Refinement Furnaces","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-22T22:18:39-07:00","id":956157,"title":"Refinement Furnaces","content":"Are these as amazing as they seem? Is there any real reason for a Promethean that has fully completed a refinement to not create one of these, ensuring they keep access to the abilities from it? They seem so much better than calcifying alembics that I'm not sure my reading was right.<br /> <br /> If this is the case, it seems like calcifying is only really useful in situations where you don't complete an entire refinement, instead only completing one or two roles before moving on.<br /> <br /> Also, can you have more than one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T23:46:38-07:00","id":956184,"title":"","content":"I was trying to figure this out too. They are indeed really good relative to calcifying, and I don't see why you couldn't have more than one, but there are some caveats: for one, I'm pretty sure you only get one chance to make an Athanor upon completing a Refinement, and if you fail the Azoth roll, you're out of luck. So getting a Furnace isn't a sure thing.<br /> <br /> Plus, you may hypothetically want to create a different Athanor type if you don't feel you're going to use Contamination much in the future or whatever. A Sanctuary or Vitriol Fount might be worthwhile for a PC.<br /> <br /> I don't have play experience yet, but I'm not sure how common it is to fully complete a refinement at one go. I guess it depends on how often you're hitting milestones, but I can easily imagine going &quot;welp, I finished Outcast and picked up Arc and Imperatus, that's all I wanted&quot; and just calcifying the alembics I want and moving on without wanting to complete Stannum.<br /> <br /> I do think the XP costs are kinda shockingly out of sync though. Considering that you get the XP you spend on calcifying alembics back if you create a Furnace, I wonder whether it's intentional that you can get a Vitriol windfall and then spend it on raising Pilgrimage for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 08-23-2016, 02:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T13:11:42-07:00","id":956509,"title":"","content":"What does everyone think about allowing willpower expenditures on these rolls to create Athanors? I don't see any real reason to disallow it, but since the default dicepool is usually small-ish, I was wondering if that seems intended or not","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T13:22:04-07:00","id":956517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/956157-refinement-furnaces?p=956509#post956509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does everyone think about allowing willpower expenditures on these rolls to create Athanors? I don't see any real reason to disallow it, but since the default dicepool is usually small-ish, I was wondering if that seems intended or not</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as your players know the rules, everything's fine. If you disallow Willpower, do you allow Steadfast? Or vice-versa? Why? I would probably allow them all as an ST because I don't see the problem in allowing your players to succeed at something important (as long as they RP the creation of the Athanor. Otherwise I become stern)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T14:12:16-07:00","id":956537,"title":"","content":"I think the Vitriol windfall is intended, it certainly makes the process of mastering a Refinement pack more of a serious punch. Also, it's good to note that all Athanor creation is a major or superlative Milestone, so you're always getting back the Vitriol you put into the creation.<br /> <br /> The thing I want to know is if in addition to the Transmutations you maintain access to the Refinement's 'Condition'. And, perhaps most importantly, can the Redeemed still use their Refinement Furnaces?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T15:51:41-07:00","id":956600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/956157-refinement-furnaces?p=956537#post956537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing I want to know is if in addition to the Transmutations you maintain access to the Refinement's 'Condition'. And, perhaps most importantly, can the Redeemed still use their Refinement Furnaces?</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess would be no to both. You would still want some way to differentiate between the Refinement you're currently on and the one you've mastered. And considering that it's a big deal that the superlative step of completing all 10 Refinements lets you keep a single Alembic, I assume you're not meant to be able to keep all your Transmutations, regardless of Athanor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T22:51:35-07:00","id":956799,"title":"","content":"Refinement Furnace says that you keep all of the benefits of the Refinement; so yes, you'd keep the Refinement Condition. And the Refinement Furnace is an item that exists apart from you, like other Athanors; <i>they</i> don't shut down when the Promethean Redeems, and I don't see a reason why <i>it</i> would be the exception. <br /> <br /> And consider that it's possible to get a Refinement Furnace even when you're trying for a different kind of Athanor (i.e., if you get an Exceptional Success on making a different kind of Athanor, you also get a Refinement Furnace). <br /> <br /> Remember though, that you need to master the Refinement before you can attempt to make a Refinement Furnace; that, not the one Vitriol, is the <i>true</i> cost of making one. As such, I wouldn't judge how good it is in comparison to calcifying Alembics; I'd judge how good it is compared to <i>other kinds of Athanors</i>. You've mastered the Refinement and are getting ready to spend the point of Vitriol on an Athanor; why would you spend it on a Firestorm Catalyst, Pilgrimage Marker, Refinement Mentor, Sanctuary, or Vitriol Fount instead of a Refinement Furnace?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T12:58:23-07:00","id":959382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/956157-refinement-furnaces?p=956799#post956799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Refinement Furnace says that you keep all of the benefits of the Refinement; so yes, you'd keep the Refinement Condition. And the Refinement Furnace is an item that exists apart from you, like other Athanors; <i>they</i> don't shut down when the Promethean Redeems, and I don't see a reason why <i>it</i> would be the exception.</div> </div> </div> </div>But likewise mortals can't make use of Athanors, and the Redeemed are mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T14:22:05-07:00","id":959470,"title":"","content":"Promethean never says that mortals can't use Athanors. Granted, most types of Athanors key off of traits that mortals don't have (Firestorm Catalyst requires you to spend a point of Pyros) or trigger aspects of Promethean existence that mortals don't have (Pilgrimage Marker sparks an Elpis Vision; Refinement Mentor lets you assume a new Role). But, for example, I could see an alchemist triggering a Firestorm Catalyst.<br /> <br /> My point is that while Athanors aren't terribly <i>useful</i> to mortals, that's not quite the same thing as Athanors being restricted to Promethean use only. In the case of Refinement Furnaces, a mortal wouldn't be able to power up the Alembics (unless he becomes an alchemist and fuels them using either Pyros from his Magnitude or Pyros harvested from a Promethean) or benefit from most Refinement Conditions (which tend to be phrased in terms of Pyros expenditures and/or Promethean features), but he <i>would</i> be able to benefit from the Persistent effects of Alembics \u2014 usually. And if he managed to master all ten Refinements (which is not the same as mastering all thirty Roles), he gains the ability to fill an Alembic with Willpower instead of Pyros; I'd be inclined to extend that benefit from the \u201cfree Alembic\u201d he gets to any Refinement Furnaces he has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}